From: BoJiang03 <bo.jiang@temple.edu>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:32:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] [MP] Resolve GQA replicas from each layer's own KV head
 count

The model-wide KV head count describes only the layers that hold it. MiMo-V2
gives its full-attention layers 4 KV heads and its sliding-window layers 8, so
at TP8 only the full layers share a head between two ranks; folding the
sliding and draft layers with the same count served one rank's head to
another. Each layer now reads its head count from the field for its type
(swa_num_key_value_heads, num_global_key_value_heads, num_key_value_heads),
draft layers from the draft config, and a layer with no declared count is
stored per rank.

Signed-off-by: BoJiang03 <bo.jiang@temple.edu>
